WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:06.904
Small nonprofits need donor support after hours. Pledge Line completes supported requests and keeps an auditable record of what happened.

2
00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:12.581
This is the working app on PayPal's sandbox. Only test funds. A masked demo PIN gates the call.

3
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:29.033
The donor asks to pause. The line reads PayPal, proposes an exact action, and waits for a separate yes.

4
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.957
That consent authorizes only this change. After execution, a fresh PayPal read confirms the gift is paused.

5
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.547
Restart requires a new proposal and another fresh yes. The line performs the action and checks PayPal again.

6
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.437
PayPal confirms active. Ending the call opens its signed receipt.

7
00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:59.446
The original verifies. A one-sentence edit is identified at sentence one.

8
00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:07.960
The buyer needs one hundred shirts within eight hundred dollars. Five PM Pacific answers a clock-time clarification while retaining earlier buying limits.

9
00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.929
Review the source-backed limits before Find a plan.

10
00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:18.176
Anthropic proposes counteroffers. Jev advises. Code checks all costs and limits across three controlled MCP suppliers.

11
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.919
No purchase is approved here. Now a read-only view of those same quote results.

12
00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:29.899
The guard selects six seventy four fifteen, below the AI candidate. The cheaper verified plan wins. Sandbox only.

13
00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:34.424
Read-only inspection of the same edited receipt. Exactly sentence one changed.

